xnu: 0086 sweet daif mask drill

drill: 0086 sweet daif mask drill

The empty stub of ml_cpu_power_enable cannot wedge in straight-line
code, yet on venus the boot dies between "P0084: processor_startup
master cpu=0 reason=1" and the entry print inside that stub - and only
on the SECOND processor_start. The only event that can kill a machine
between two adjacent statements is an asynchronous exception, most
plausibly the just-rearmed vtimer PPI27 firing (the cpu already has
IRQs enabled at this point) or an SError.

Drill: around the call, mask IRQ/FIQ/SError/Debug via DAIF, dump
ISR_EL1 before and after (isr bits: I=1 IRQ pending, F FIQ, A SError),
then re-enable DAIF immediately after the call. Expected evidence:
- pre prints, post does not   -> impossible straight-line, console lock
- post prints, end does not   -> unmasking delivers the killer, i.e.
                                async exception confirmed
- everything prints, wedge moved elsewhere -> async path confirmed

diff --git a/osfmk/kern/processor.c b/osfmk/kern/processor.c
index 7254b06..008600a 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/processor.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/processor.c
@@ -806,7 +806,29 @@ processor_startup(
 		kprintf("P0084: processor_startup master cpu=%d reason=%d\n",
 		    processor->cpu_id, reason);
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+		{
+			uint64_t daif = __builtin_arm_rsr64("DAIF");
+			uint64_t isr = __builtin_arm_rsr64("ISR_EL1");
+
+			/* 0086 wedge drill: see file header. Mask everything
+			 * around the empty-stub call; a death in this window
+			 * with DAIF closed can only be console/SPL state. */
+			__asm__ volatile("msr daifset, #0xf; dmb ish; isb" ::: "memory");
+			kprintf("P0086: master pre: daif=%llx isr=%llx (masked now)\n",
+			    daif, isr);
+		}
+#endif
 		ml_cpu_power_enable(processor->cpu_id);
 		kprintf("P0084: processor_startup master: ml_cpu_power_enable returned\n");
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+		{
+			uint64_t isr = __builtin_arm_rsr64("ISR_EL1");
+
+			kprintf("P0086: master post: isr=%llx -> about to unmask\n", isr);
+			__asm__ volatile("msr daifclr, #0xf; dmb ish; isb" ::: "memory");
+			kprintf("P0086: master end: DAIF unmasked ok\n");
+		}
+#endif
 #else
 		ml_cpu_power_enable(processor->cpu_id);
 #endif

